        "id": "p10-q60-62-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{10}\\sec\\frac{2\\pi}{5}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$",
          "worked": "Since $\\frac{\\pi}{10}+\\frac{2\\pi}{5}=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, the angles are complementary.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{10}\\sec\\frac{2\\pi}{5}&=\\frac{\\sin(\\pi/10)}{\\cos(2\\pi/5)}\\\\\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{10}\\sec\\frac{2\\pi}{5}&=\\frac{\\sin(\\pi/10)}{\\sin(\\pi/10)}\\\\\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{10}\\sec\\frac{2\\pi}{5}&=1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q60-62-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{8}-\\sin\\frac{3\\pi}{8}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$",
          "worked": "Since $\\frac{\\pi}{8}+\\frac{3\\pi}{8}=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, the angles are complementary.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{8}-\\sin\\frac{3\\pi}{8}&=\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{8}-\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\\\\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{8}-\\sin\\frac{3\\pi}{8}&=0\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q60-62-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$2\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\tan\\frac{7\\pi}{16}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$",
          "worked": "Since $\\frac{\\pi}{16}+\\frac{7\\pi}{16}=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, the angles are complementary.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\tan\\frac{7\\pi}{16}&=2\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\cot\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\\\2\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\tan\\frac{7\\pi}{16}&=2\\frac{\\sin(\\pi/16)}{\\cos(\\pi/16)}\\frac{\\cos(\\pi/16)}{\\sin(\\pi/16)}\\\\2\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\tan\\frac{7\\pi}{16}&=2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
